# b2-innsbruck-defend: the battle of session 9 (Innsbruck, 1805), played by the Allies, who
# defend. Every unit of the player rests, each turn, until the time is up; the computer's
# French attack. The battle's BATTLE.$$$ is b2-innsbruck-defend.battle.
# seed 1 (NAP_SEED)

# A TICK of a second or more: any key ends it. A "hit a key" pause: a space. A unit's
# order: a space, which rests it.
rule 3 key f12
rule 1 key space
# The combat menu of a unit of the player that fights: Enter, the first item (Light Skirmish).
rule 2:C key enter
play until 5
# shot first-order
state
key space
rule 5 key space
# over writes OUTCOME.&&& and waits at place 7 before it exits (scriptend).
play until 7
# shot result
state
key f12
